--- a/.andromeda/test-plan.md
+++ b/.andromeda/test-plan.md
@@ -1062,2 +1062,3 @@
 decision/doctest-only-catch-is-missed · Doctest-only catch counts as missed — A mutant caught only by a doctest counts as missed, and the missing unit test must be added.
+decision/equivalent-survivors-known-limit · Two equivalent survivors are a known limit — Two equivalent mutants, one widening the ask capture read to the PreToolUse it found, one adding the window at the modal row to the box-below read, survive every test and stand beside the peer admission survivor as known limits, read at each epoch-boundary audit. · why: No input separates either mutant, and the code is not reshaped to kill one.
 decision/fake-agent-own-process-group · Fake agent spawns in its own process group — Every command the fake agent spawns runs in a process group of its own. · why: A killed wrapper's PTY hangup would reach hooks cut off in their exit-time profile write, leaving profiles llvm-profdata refuses.
@@ -1151,2 +1152,3 @@
 decision/fuzz-toolchain-single-source · Fuzz toolchain from one source — The fuzz toolchain channel is read from the fuzz workspace's own toolchain file, the one source, and the fuzz dir is a separate cargo workspace excluded from the root.
+decision/harness-abort-wait-below-ci-kill · Harness abort wait below the ci kill — After a failed readiness the harness boot waits at most 15 s for its abort, so a stuck boot ends within 17 s, below the 20 s ci per-test kill of the harness lifecycle binary; the 20 s readiness bound per instance stays.
 decision/harness-builds-in-its-own-target · Harness builds into its own target dir — The harness build always uses its own target dir, never the target dir the shim's cargo run uses. · why: a running harness binary could not be relinked, and a workspace-wide build re-fingerprints it
@@ -1336,3 +1338,3 @@
 decision/verify-driven-tests-20s-kill · Per-test kill bounds verify-driven tests — A test that drives viola verify has no test-side bound on that call; its binary sits on the ci override whose 20 s per-test kill is its bound. · why: Ratified; sized from the measured verify floor plus a 3x runner tail; one verify stamp taken per build keeps each stamped-home test under it.
-decision/verify-window-80s-kill · 80 s kill for the verify_window_ class — Tests named verify_window_ take an 80 s per-test kill, in both the ci and mutants profiles, through an override that stands first. · why: Their cases wait out the gate's 8.5 s maximum several times by design. · guard: mutants_verify_window_override_stands_before_the_harness_package_override
+decision/verify-window-80s-kill · 80 s kill for the verify_window_ class — Tests named verify_window_, and the fake agent dialog and framing replay tests over every recorded set, take an 80 s per-test kill, in both the ci and mutants profiles, through an override that stands first. · why: Their cases wait out the gate's 8.5 s maximum several times by design. · guard: mutants_verify_window_override_stands_before_the_harness_package_override
 decision/viola-e2e-30s-mutants-kill · 30 s mutants kill for the harness package — Under the mutants profile the viola-e2e package takes a 30 s per-test kill. · why: The harness's own tests wait out its 20 s boot deadline by design.
